"Internal Error ()\nciteturn12view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn10search0\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://help.udio.com/en/articles/12683565-changes-associated-with-the-universal-music-group-umg-partnership: (400) Timeout fetching\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUdio - Warner Music Group (WMG) partnership | Udio Help Center (https://help.udio.com/en/articles/12874375-udio-warner-music-group-wmg-partnership)\nciteturn12view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn9search0\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 48\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Update subscription or account†udio.com】【2†See what's new】【3†Check Udio site status†status.udio.com】\nL3: \nL4: 【1†Update subscription or account†udio.com】【2†See what's new】【3†Check Udio site status†status.udio.com】\nL5: \nL6: Search for articles...[Input: Search for articles...]\nL7: \nL8:   1. 【4†All Collections】\nL9: \nL10:   2. 【5†Miscellaneous】\nL11: \nL12:   3. Udio - Warner Music Group (WMG) partnership\nL13: # Udio - Warner Music Group (WMG) partnership\nL14: \nL15: November 19, 2025\nL16: \nL17: Udio and Warner Music Group (WMG) are collaborating on Udio’s next-generation AI music service through a new licensing arrangement. This arrangement additionally resolves the companies’ copyright litigation.\nL18: Udio’s reimagined platform will introduce a suite of creative experiences that enable users to make remixes, covers, and new songs using the voices and styles of artists who choose to participate. Crucially, the collaboration will generate new revenue streams for artists and songwriters, while providing safeguards and usage guardrails for participating musicians.\nL19: \nL20: We here at team Udio are incredibly excited to build this next chapter. Onwards and upwards!\nL21: \nL22: Did the labels buy Udio / do they own Udio?\nL23: No, they did not. Udio has entered into licensing agreements with Warner and Universal to train new models based on their data and to work with their artists.\nL24: \nL25: Why have you partnered with WMG (and previously Universal Music Group)?\nL26: \nL27: We wanted to enable more powerful and appealing opportunities for Udio creators over the long haul while also supporting the rights of longtime traditional artists. We believe that partnering with artists, songwriters, and rightsholders is the best way to accomplish this.\nL28: Does the Warner announcement change anything about how I use Udio today?\nL29: \nL30: No. Udio is still governed by 【6†our transition ToS†www.udio.com】 that was put into place on 29 October.\nL31: \nL32: What does this mean for songs I’m making today?\nL33: \nL34: During this transition…\nL35: \nL36:   * You still have access to the same v1, v1.5, and v1.5 Allegro models.\nL37: \nL38:   * You can use the same core creation tools as well, such as extend, remix, Styles, etc.\nL39:   * And lastly, you can keep sharing your Udio songs with others through 【7†udio.com†udio.com】 URLs, which anyone – even non-Udio users – can access.\nL40: \nL41: Did this answer your question?\nL42: \nL43: Disappointed Reaction😞Neutral Reaction😐Smiley Reaction😃\nL44: \nL45: 【4†Udio Help Center】\nL46: \nL47:   *   *   *   *   * 【8†We run on Intercom†www.intercom.com】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCreate a Song with Your Own Lyrics | Udio Help Center (https://help.udio.com/en/articles/10716221-create-a-song-with-your-own-lyrics)\nciteturn12view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn9search2\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 84\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Update subscription or account†udio.com】【2†See what's new】【3†Check Udio site status†status.udio.com】\nL3: \nL4: 【1†Update subscription or account†udio.com】【2†See what's new】【3†Check Udio site status†status.udio.com】\nL5: \nL6: Search for articles...[Input: Search for articles...]\nL7: \nL8:   1. 【4†All Collections】\nL9: \nL10:   2. 【5†Song Creation】\nL11: \nL12:   3. Create a Song with Your Own Lyrics\nL13: # Create a Song with Your Own Lyrics\nL14: \nL15: March 14, 2025\nL16: \nL17: Writing your own lyrics lets you tell stories, express emotions, and bring personal meaning to your music. Whether you want to generate lyrics quickly or craft them from scratch, here’s how to do it.\nL18: \nL19: ## Generate Lyrics from a Song Description\nL20: \nL21: Need inspiration? Describe your song’s theme, and Udio will generate lyrics for you.\nL22: ## How to Generate Lyrics:\nL23: \nL24:   1. Go to the Home Page or Create Page.\nL25: \nL26:   2. In the Prompt field, describe your song’s story or mood.\nL27: \nL28: Example prompts:\nL29: \nL30:     Walking on the beach under a sunny rain, synthwave, edm\nL31: \nL32:     My friend always tries to outdo me, rock opera\nL33: \nL34:     I found a coin dropped by my favorite anime character, j-pop\nL35: \nL36:   3. Udio will generate lyrics, which you can hear when your song is created.\nL37: \nL38: 💡 Try different descriptions to explore unique lyric ideas!\nL39: ## Use the Extended Editor for More Control\nL40: \nL41: Want to refine your lyrics before finalizing? The Extended Editor lets you tweak and explore different ideas.\nL42: \nL43: ## How to Use the Extended Editor:\nL44: \nL45:   1. Go to the Create Page.\nL46: \nL47:   2. Write Your Lyrics, select Custom.\nL48: \nL49:   3. Enter a song description and click \"Write for me\".\nL50: \nL51: 💡 Not satisfied? Click \"Regenerate Lyrics\" to try again.\nL52: ## Extra Features:\nL53: \nL54:   * Go Back – Revisit previous versions.\nL55: \nL56:   * Move Forward – Return to the latest version.\nL57: \nL58:   * View History – See past lyric generations.\nL59: \nL60:   * Edit Lyrics – Manually adjust and refine in the text editor.\nL61: \nL62: ## Use Your Own Custom Lyrics\nL63: \nL64: Already have lyrics? Add them directly for full creative control!\nL65: ## How to Add Your Own Lyrics:\nL66: \nL67:   1. Go to the Create Page.\nL68: \nL69:   2. Write Your Lyrics, select Custom.\nL70: \nL71:   3. Type or paste your lyrics into the Lyrics Editor.\nL72: \nL73: Now you’re ready to turn your words into music!\nL74: \nL75: Next ➡️ 【6†Share Your Song】\nL76: \nL77: Did this answer your question?\nL78: \nL79: Disappointed Reaction😞Neutral Reaction😐Smiley Reaction😃\nL80: \nL81: 【4†Udio Help Center】\nL82: \nL83:   *   *   *   *   * 【7†We run on Intercom†www.intercom.com】\n"